#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:6
msgid "Monitoring for parameter changes (Python)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:8
msgid ""
"**Goal:** Learn to use the ParameterEventHandler class to monitor and "
"respond to parameter changes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:10
msgid "**Tutorial level:** Intermediate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:12
msgid "**Time:** 20 minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:16
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:19
msgid "Background"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/ROS-Framework/parameters/Working-with-parameters/Monitoring-For-Parameter-Changes-Python.rst:21
msgid ""
"Often a node needs to respond to changes to its own parameters or another "
"node's parameters. The ParameterEventHandler class makes it easy to listen "
"for parameter changes so that your code can respond to them. This tutorial "
"will show you how to use the Python version of the ParameterEventHandler "
"class to monitor for changes to a node's own parameters as well as changes "
"to another node's parameters."
msgstr ""

